      "content": "i get the upskilling thing but let's be real—if an AI can do a job 10x faster or cheaper, it doesn't make much sense to keep the human around just to be \"compassionate.\" if i'm looking at the bottom line, isn't the most logical move to just automate the roles that are most expensive or inefficient?",
